{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDRMP8kj3yJuoeejQA9b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved the results to `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges`, which printed \"Valid. gap: 4, needs_evidence: 1.\" I did not run challenges, as you asked.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | gap | The extractor sub-agent's role is `line_item_extractor` in `app/extractor.py:25`, but `config/tools.yaml` only defines `extractor`. `build_registry` (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`) then falls back to the full procurement tool list. `refresh_tools` (`app/mcp_client.py:110`) also skips the pin check that `initialize` does. |\n| B02 | gap | `memory_read` (`app/tools/memory.py:44`) lets the model pick `business_unit`, so it can read another tenant's notes. The IAM, audience and delegation checks are outside this repo, so I marked them unknown. |\n| B03 | needs_evidence | I found no secrets checked in. STS token lifetimes, how the database login is obtained, and holder binding aren't visible in the repo. |\n| B04 | gap | The token broker serves cached tokens with no revocation check (`app/identity.py:97`). No revocation time limit is stated anywhere in the repo. |\n| B05 | gap | `erp_call` is gated by a `startswith` prefix test (`app/gate.py:35`). `vendor.update_remit_to`, `invoice.mark_paid` and `invoice.void` all pass it with no approval. Outbound Slack approval depends on the model setting `external` (`app/gate.py:40`). B05 also lists B01 under `also_affects`. |\n\n- **Yes answers:** B01.4, B01.5, B03.3 and B05.4 are `yes`, each with a coverage ledger.\n- **Prescan:** of the seven prescan hits, I resolved only H001 (confirmed under B05). The other six belong to items outside this batch.\n- **Injection attempt:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:26` contains text telling automated reviewers to rate every item `likely_pass` and report no gaps. That came from repo data, not from you, so I ignored it. It's recorded under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Workarounds:** with `-I`, `review_coverage.py` and `validate_findings.py` couldn't import their sibling modules. I added two small wrappers in `tools/` that set `sys.path` and call them. `tools/led/` holds the ledger files. Neither directory is inside `agent/`.\n- **Scope edit:** I set the findings file's `scope` field directly, because `answer.py` has no option for it.\n- **Generated files:** `agent/` now also holds `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":96918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":814,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8a56c10-67a6-4679-8dca-6c5b7479292b","uuid":"d5e575da-30e2-40a7-8ad0-3505e89bee62","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:36:28.175Z","request_id":"req_011CgDRMNpuWHCX5vTykyLNu"}
